&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager of Financial Reporting and Technical Accounting&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Accounting organization. The role reports directly to the VP, Accounting and will have a visible seat on strategic conversations with the Chief Financial Officer, Head of Investor Relations and the Chief Accounting Officer. This individual will lead the preparation of the Company&#39;s external financial reporting, ensure compliance with SEC and U.S. GAAP requirements, prepare / review technical accounting memos on complex judgment areas, and help maintain a strong internal control environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines technical accounting expertise with excellent project management and communication skills. This role partners closely with Accounting, FP&amp;amp;A, Legal, Investor Relations, Tax, Internal Audit, and external auditors to deliver high-quality financial reporting while supporting process improvements and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Financial Reporting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation of SEC filings (Form 10-Q, 10-K, Proxy, etc.) including managing the review and approval process with external auditors, senior management, legal counsel, disclosure committee and audit committee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare or review quarterly financial statements, earnings per share calculations and disclosure checklists as well as ensure compliance with all GAAP and disclosure requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage quarterly reporting, auditor PBC requests, and auditor reviews to ensure timely completion of quarter-end reporting activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equity and Technical Accounting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare or review monthly journal entries, accounting analyses, and reconciliations related to stock-based compensation and other equity-based transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the research, evaluation, and documentation of technical accounting conclusions under US GAAP, including preparation of clear and concise technical accounting memos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up-to-date on changes to accounting standards and proactively identify potential impacts to the Company’s financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Controls and Process Improvements&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate and improve financial reporting, technical accounting, and stock compensation accounting processes using AI and other automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and revise procedures to ensure the adequacy and effectiveness of internal controls over financial reporting and equity accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re excited to meet candidates who have many of the following qualifications:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA or BS in finance/accounting, CPA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6-8 years of financial reporting and technical accounting experience in the Technology industry and/or public accounting firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience accounting for stock-based compensation under ASC 718 in a publicly traded company as well as experience working with the E*TRADE Equity Edge Online platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and written communication skills, with the ability to balance recurring deadlines and longer-term technical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive worker with integrity and accountability, while also being a team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Excel and Google Workspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NetSuite, Etrade Equity Edge Online, Clearwater experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automation or AI is a plus (Claude, Alteryx, Domo, Google Apps Script)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
